{"“Can’t do it, Findle; I’m with somebody else! Call me up to-morrow about \003one o’clock\004!”","This Side of Paradise","F. Scott Fitzgerald",true},
{"“About \003one o’clock\004 they moved to Maxim’s, and two found them in Deviniere’s. Sloane had been drinking consecutively and was in a state of unsteady exhilaration, but Amory was quite tiresomely sober; they had run across none of those ancient, corrupt buyers of champagne who usually assisted their New York parties.”","This Side of Paradise","F. Scott Fitzgerald",true},
{"The more he thought about it the more puzzled he was… He didn’t understand this revolver\nbusiness…\nSomebody in the house had got that revolver…\nDownstairs a clock \003struck one\004.","And Then There Were None","Agatha Christie",true},
{"\0031:00 am.\004 I felt the surrounding quietness suffocating me.","Sister","Rosamund Lupton",true},
{"He didn’t know what was at the end of the chute. The opening was narrow (though large enough to take the canary). He dreamed that the chute opened onto vast garbage bins filled with old coffee filters, ravioli in tomato sauce and mangled genitalia. Huge worms, as big as the canary, armed with terrible beaks, would attack the body. Tear off the feet, rip out its intestines, burst the eyeballs. He woke up, trembling; it was only \003one o’clock\004. He swallowed three Xanax. So ended his first night of freedom.","Atomised","Michel Houellebecq",false},
{"I’m the only one awake in this house on this night before the day that will change all our lives. Though it’s already that day: the little luminous hands on my alarm clock (which I haven’t set) show just gone \003one in the morning\004.","Tomorrow","Graham Swift",true},
{"It was the thirtieth of May by now. \003One am\004 on the thirtieth of May 1940. Quite a famous date on which to be lying awake and staring at the ceiling. Already in the creeks and tidal estuaries of England the pleasure-boats and paddle-steamers were casting their moorings for the day trip to Dunkirk. And, over on the other side, Ted stood as a good a chance as anyone else.","London Belongs to Me","Norman Collins",true},
{"Last night of all, When yon same star that’s westward from the pole Had made his course t’illume that part of heaven Where now it burns, Marcellus and myself, \003The bell then beating one\004.","Hamlet","William Shakespeare",true},
